The function `processImageBatch` processes a batch of images concurrently, up to a maximum number defined by `MAX_CONCURRENT_TASKS`. It dynamically adjusts memory allocation based on the current usage and enforces a limit to prevent integer overflow. The example usage shows how to call this function with an array of image tasks.']

